<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

Problem summary:
The app is failing to generate images due to three issues observed in console logs:
1) Uncaught TypeError: TemplateManager.generateImages is not a function — main.js registers a click handler that calls TemplateManager.generateImages without checking it exists, causing an uncaught exception in some contexts.
2) Pollinations requests return HTTP 429 (Too Many Requests). pollinations.generateOne currently only retries on 502/503/504; 429 responses are treated as fatal and not retried. Also, response headers/content-type are not logged which makes debugging difficult.
3) Stability backup fails with 400 (Bad Request) but stability.js does not log response body when non-OK, making diagnosis harder.

Goals for PR:
- Prevent uncaught TypeError by guarding TemplateManager.generateImages calls in js/core/main.js.
- Treat 429 responses from Pollinations as retryable with a longer exponential/backoff delay, and add more diagnostic logs (response.type, response.headers.get('content-type'), response.url) after fetch so we can see whether responses are opaque or HTML error pages.
- Improve stability.js logging to capture response.text() when response.ok is false to reveal API error details.

Files to modify:
1) js/core/main.js
  - Change the generate button click handler so it checks window.TemplateManager and typeof TemplateManager.generateImages === 'function' before calling. If missing, log an error and show a user-facing message via UI.showMessage if available.

2) js/features/generation/pollinations.js
  - After the fetch() call, add a console.log that outputs response.status, response.type, response.url and response.headers.get('content-type').
  - In the non-ok response handling, treat HTTP 429 as retryable. Use a longer backoff for 429 (10-20 seconds) and retry up to the configured retries count. Keep existing retry behavior for 502/503/504 but consolidate handling into a single branch for retryable statuses.

3) js/features/generation/stability.js
  - When Stability API returns non-ok, read response.text() and log it along with response.status. Ensure that any thrown Error includes the status and response body to aid debugging.

Implementation details / code snippets to apply (exact intended changes):

A) js/core/main.js — replace the generate button handler with:

