Refactors the container-vm module to support multiple containers using a structured `containers` map variable, similar to Chainguard's terraform-infra-common module.

### Changes

- **variables.tf**: Replace individual container variables with a `containers` map accepting `image`, `command`, `args`, `env`, and `restart_policy` per container
- **cloud-init.yaml.tftpl**: Generate separate systemd service for each container in the map
- **main.tf**: Pass containers map to template

### Usage

```hcl
module "vm" {
  source = "./container-vm"

  project_id            = "my-project"
  service_account_email = "sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com"
  network               = "my-network"
  subnetwork            = "my-subnet"

  containers = {
    app = {
      image = "gcr.io/my-project/app@sha256:abc123..."
      env = [
        { name = "PORT", value = "8080" }
      ]
    }
    sidecar = {
      image          = "gcr.io/my-project/sidecar@sha256:def456..."
      args           = ["--verbose"]
      restart_policy = "on-failure"
    }
  }
}
```

All container images must be referenced by digest. Each container runs as an independent systemd service.

